					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/440-hertz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1249440); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1249440&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606360669" alt="440 Hertz" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1249440)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/440-hertz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1249440); return false;" >440 Hertz</a></span> <span class="odate time_1547932549 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Jan 2019 21:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4124297">
									

<p>I like the idea, unexpectedly wholesome and fun! But there are a bunch of sentences that are phrased weird, it broke my immersion&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;A&nbsp;few&nbsp;examples,&nbsp;and&nbsp;my&nbsp;opinion&nbsp;on&nbsp;why&nbsp;it&nbsp;sounds&nbsp;awkward</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Use of SCP-2541 is restricted to personnel with clearance below Level-2</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wouldn't it be restricted to ABOVE (or &quot;personnel [&#8230;] are restricted FROM using [&#8230;]&quot;)? Or is senior staff hornier, thus creating a need to limit their access lest they develop an addiction?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>all feature an icon of a stylized yellow lemon somewhere on its packaging</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It should be &quot;on their packaging&quot;, shouldn't it?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>[subjects] report the feeling of intercourse [&#8230;] as feeling &quot;incredibly realistic&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Double feeling! The second one is unneeded. (&quot;subjects report the feeling of intercourse [&#8230;] to be incredibly realistic&quot;).<br />
Also using quotation marks makes it sounds like all subjects worded it the same way, with the word &quot;incredibly&quot;&#8230; If it's a citation from one subject, maybe &quot;The feeling has been reported&quot; would work better than &quot;Subjects report&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>ceasing the cognitohazardous effect upon affected subjects</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;ceasing upon&quot; doesn't sound valid, how about &quot;lifting from&quot; maybe?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>expresses repeated inappropriate or unwanted behavior upon</p>
</blockquote>
<p>same, why not &quot;show inappropriate behavior towards&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'd guess that most people in the Foundation that would rather keep their kinks private.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Stray &quot;that&quot;!</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>But the story is good, promoting consent and sex-positivity is always nice, and the security guard and Bobs are really likeable!</p>

							</div>

								
					
